    <Options>
      <Main applyHouseholdOperatingConditions="false" applyReducedOperatingConditions="false" atypicalElectricalLoads="false" waterConservation="true" referenceHouse="false" greenerHomesTab="false">
        <Vermiculite code="3">
          <English>No Vermiculite</English>
          <French>Pas de Vermiculite</French>
        </Vermiculite>
      </Main>
      <WaterConservation LowFlushToilets="2" LowFlushToiletsUpgrade="0" />
      <RURComments xml:space="preserve">
                <airSeal>The infiltration test has shown air leakage from the following house components:
-	Exterior doors
-	Receptacles
-	Electrical panel
-	Header perimeter floor joist
-	Fireplace
-	Furnace chimney
During the infiltration test walkthrough, we notice air leakage on the items listed above. Airtightness is very important to achieve energy savings.
</airSeal>
                <mainWalls>At the time of the assessment, the insulation of the exterior walls was R-12. We recommend upgrading the insulation level. You are eligible for $2.50/square foot for the addition of R-20+, and $ 3.50/square foot for R-30+. </mainWalls>
                <ceilingsCathedral>At the time of the audit, the insulation level of the attic was estimated to be R-40. We recommend adding insulation to meet the city of Whitehorse standard of R-60.</ceilingsCathedral>
                <foundation>We recommend adding insulation on the foundation walls and the header joist (perimeter joist). Insulating the basement will contribute directly to energy savings.  </foundation>
                <windows>We recommend the replacement of the windows by triple pane and Energy Star certified units with Lowe coating and Argon filled.</windows>
                <doors>We recommend the replacement of the wood doors with new energy star certified products.  </doors>
                <VentilationSystem>We recommend the installation of an HRV (Heat Recovery Ventilator) HVI (Home Ventilation Institute) and Energy Star certified, to ensure proper ventilation inside your home.</VentilationSystem>
                <HeatingSystem>ETS PROGRAM
For more information concerning the Electrical Thermal Storage Unit, please follow the link below:
http://yukonconservation.org/programs/energy/electric-thermal-storage#:~:text=Electric%20thermal%20storage%20(ETS)%20is,providing%20heat%20throughout%20the%20day 
</HeatingSystem>
            </RURComments>
      <GreenerHomes basementSlabInsulated="true" moistureProofCrawlSpace="true" waterproofing="true" roofingMembrane="false" minR10ContinuousExposedFloors="false" backwaterValve="true" sumpPump="true" smartThermostats="true" remoteCommunities="true" evaluationCost="50">
